ded\">your favorite brand</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1.5</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cups</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">chicken broth</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">low sodium recommended</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">3</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cloves</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">garlic</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">minced</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">0.5</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">finely chopped onion</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">adds flavor</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">grated Parmesan cheese</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for a creamy finish</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">to taste</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">0.5</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">ground black pepper</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for seasoning</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">chopped fresh parsley</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for garnish</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-5439-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"5439\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 6-quart crockpot&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For cooking the chicken and pasta</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-5439-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-5439-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"5439\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5439-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Place the chicken breasts in the bottom of a 6-quart crockpot.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5439-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Pour the minced garlic, chopped onion, salt, and pepper over the chicken.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5439-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Add the chicken broth and cover; cook on LOW for 4–5 hours or on HIGH for 2–3 hours.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5439-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Remove the chicken and shred with two forks; return shredded chicken to the crockpot.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5439-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Stir in the Alfredo sauce, grated Parmesan, and dry pasta until well combined.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5439-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 6: Cover and cook on HIGH for 30–45 minutes, stirring halfway through, until the pasta is tender.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-5439-step-0-6\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 7: Garnish with chopped parsley before serving.</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-5439-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>450</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>15g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>30g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>50g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here&#8217;s what you&#8217;ll need to make your delicious CROCKPOT CHICKEN ALFREDO PASTA!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ingredients-for-CROCKPOT-CHICKEN-ALFREDO-PASTA.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for CROCKPOT CHICKEN ALFREDO PASTA displayed on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-5437\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ingredients-for-CROCKPOT-CHICKEN-ALFREDO-PASTA.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ingredients-for-CROCKPOT-CHICKEN-ALFREDO-PASTA-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>4 boneless skinless chicken breasts</strong> – fresh or thawed</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>3 cups dry penne </strong><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pasta\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>pasta</strong> </a>– uncooked</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 jar (15 oz) Alfredo sauce</strong> – your favorite brand</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1½ cups chicken broth</strong> – low sodium recommended</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>3 cloves garlic</strong> – minced</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>½ cup finely chopped onion</strong> – adds flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 cup grated Parmesan cheese</strong> – for a creamy finish</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 teaspoon salt</strong> – to taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>½ teaspoon ground black pepper</strong> – for seasoning</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tablespoons chopped fresh parsley</strong> – for garnish</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-crockpot-chicken-alfredo-pasta\"><strong>How to Make CROCKPOT CHICKEN ALFREDO PASTA</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This delightful CROCKPOT CHICKEN ALFREDO PASTA is a breeze to prepare! With a prep time of just 15 minutes and a cooking time of 4–5 hours on LOW or 2–3 hours on HIGH, you can set it and forget it. Plus, an extra 30–45 minutes on HIGH for the pasta to cook makes this dish a comforting meal that’s perfect for busy days.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Preparation-Steps-for-CROCKPOT-CHICKEN-ALFREDO-PASTA.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step preparation of CROCKPOT CHICKEN ALFREDO PASTA, including chicken in a crockpot, added seasonings, chicken broth, and the final garnished dish.\" class=\"wp-image-5438\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Preparation-Steps-for-CROCKPOT-CHICKEN-ALFREDO-PASTA.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Preparation-Steps-for-CROCKPOT-CHICKEN-ALFREDO-PASTA-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Place the Chicken</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Place the chicken breasts in the bottom of a 6-quart crockpot.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Add Seasonings</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Pour the minced garlic, chopped onion, salt, and pepper over the chicken.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Add Chicken Broth</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add the chicken broth and cover; cook on LOW for 4–5 hours or on HIGH for 2–3 hours.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Shred the Chicken</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Remove the chicken and shred with two forks; return shredded chicken to the crockpot.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Mix in Alfredo Sauce</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Stir in the Alfredo sauce, grated Parmesan, and dry pasta until well combined.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Cook the Pasta</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cover and cook on HIGH for 30–45 minutes, stirring halfway through, until the pasta is tender.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Garnish and Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Garnish with chopped parsley before serving.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Main Course</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>Italian</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>240 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>45 minutes for pasta to cook</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>300 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Contains chicken and dairy</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Hot and creamy with parsley garnish</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-crockpot-chicken-alfredo-pasta\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making CROCKPOT CHICKEN ALFREDO PASTA</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Use boneless, skinless chicken thighs for extra tenderness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Opt for whole wheat or gluten-free pasta for a healthier twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add fresh spinach or broccoli in the last hour for a pop of color and nutrition.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Stir in cream cheese or Greek yogurt for a creamier sauce.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with freshly grated Parmesan just before serving for a burst of flavor.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-crockpot-chicken-alfredo-pasta\"><strong>How to Serve this CROCKPOT CHICKEN ALFREDO PASTA</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Garnish with fresh parsley or basil for a pop of color.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with a side of garlic bread for dipping.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a crisp green salad drizzled with lemon vinaigrette.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with grated Parmesan cheese for extra flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Mix in steamed broccoli or spinach for added nutrition.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Offer a sprinkle of red pepper flakes for a spicy kick.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve in bowls with crusty bread on the side for a cozy meal.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can easily prepare and store your CROCKPOT CHICKEN ALFREDO PASTA:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing CROCKPOT CHICKEN ALFREDO PASTA Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow the pasta to cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Transfer leftovers to an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3-4 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing CROCKPOT CHICKEN ALFREDO PASTA</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Cool the pasta completely before freezing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use freezer-safe containers or bags for storage.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 2-3 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating CROCKPOT CHICKEN ALFREDO PASTA</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw overnight in the refrigerator if frozen.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat in a saucepan over low heat, adding a splash of milk for creaminess.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Stir frequently until heated through.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Microwave in short intervals, stirring in between, if preferred.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. Can I put uncooked pasta in a crockpot?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, you can put uncooked pasta in a crockpot! However, it&#8217;s best to add it during the last 30 minutes of cooking to prevent it from becoming mushy. Make sure to stir it well and add enough liquid to ensure it cooks properly and absorbs the flavors of the sauce.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. Is it okay to put raw chicken in a slow cooker?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Absolutely! You can put raw chicken in a slow cooker. The slow cooking process ensures that the chicken cooks thoroughly and remains tender. Just make sure to cook it for the recommended time to ensure it&#8217;s safe to eat.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. Can you cook pasta in sauce in a crockpot?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, you can cook pasta in sauce in a crockpot! Just be mindful of the cooking time and add the pasta towards the end of the cooking process to avoid overcooking. This method allows the pasta to absorb the flavors of the sauce beautifully.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. How to cook chicken pasta in a slow cooker?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To cook chicken pasta in a slow cooker, start by adding your raw chicken, seasonings, and sauce to the pot. Cook on low for several hours until the chicken is tender. Then, add uncooked pasta during the last 30 minutes of cooking, ensuring there&#8217;s enough liquid for it to cook properly. Stir well and enjoy your delicious meal!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We hope you’re as excited to try this Crockpot Chicken Alfredo Pasta as we are! It’s a simple, comforting dish that brings back memories of family dinners and cozy nights in. So grab your ingredients, set that slow cooker, and let the magic happen. Enjoy every creamy, delicious bite—you deserve it!</p>\n",
  "ingredients": [
    "4 pieces boneless skinless chicken breasts (fresh or thawed)",
    "3 cups dry penne pasta (uncooked)",
    "1 jar (15 oz) Alfredo sauce (your favorite brand)",
    "1.5 cups chicken broth (low sodium recommended)",
    "3 cloves garlic (minced)",
    "0.5 cup finely chopped onion (adds flavor)",
    "1 cup grated Parmesan cheese (for a creamy finish)",
    "1 teaspoon salt (to taste)",
    "0.5 teaspoon ground black pepper (for seasoning)",
    "2 tablespoons chopped fresh parsley (for garnish)"
  ],
